  "vector_memory": {
    "semantic_summary": "MeshRendererBehaviour is a specialized rendering service extending RendererBehaviour, dedicated to handling physically-based rendering (PBR) for mesh objects. It manages complex state by binding various texture maps—such as normal, specular, roughness, AO, and emissive maps—to the WebGL context. The core logic in the draw() method integrates scene data like SceneFog and utilizes Camera state for correct transformation and shading during rendering."
  },
